# HG changeset patch
# User Welpy-cw <58345540+Welpy-cw@users.noreply.github.com>
# Date 1794266063 -7200
# Node ID bb1e61b410a1be385980450efb34de6441eb1e1d
# Parent  130a410d00bbb80f23354b96431db0cd5ec9a866
Bug 1802096 - Show item counts when dragging multiple attachments or messages. r=aleca

Render a system-colored, high-DPI-aware stack and count badge for multi-item
drags in the reader, composer, message list, and Search Messages. Retain
existing single-item feedback.

Consolidate attachment transfer setup and file promises in DragUtils. Give
each drag its own attachment map and macOS duplicate-save tracking, adapt
composer attachments for saving, and honor the exported filename. Use the
default isTmp flag so saved attachments appear in Downloads.

Use the current database-view selection API in Search Messages so dragging
exports the selected results.

Add browser coverage for preview counts and scaling, skipped and deleted
attachments, search results, and real promised-file saves, including filename
collisions and repeated drags.

Validation: commlint and headless preview and reader attachment tests pass.
The existing composer drag test is skipped on Linux.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336767

